Experiment 6(a)
Title: Write a shell script that determines the period for which a specified user is working on the system.

Steps:
Open the Ubuntu terminal.  
Create a shell script: nano user.sh  
Enter the required shell script to check the specified user's login/working time.  
Save and exit the file: Ctrl + O, Enter, Ctrl + X  
Give execution permission: chmod +x user.sh (or execute using bash user.sh student / ./user.sh student).  
Execute the script by passing the username: ./user.sh student  
The script displays the user's login time if the user is currently logged in.  


Script used-

#!/bin/bash
read -p "Enter username: " user
login_time=$(who | awk -v u="$user" '$1 == u {print $3, $4; exit}')

if [ -z "$login_time" ]
then
    echo "User is not currently logged in."
else
    echo "Login time : $login_time"
fi


Result:
Successfully determined the login / working period information of the specified user.
